and never up. * [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_max_clients","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_unused_client_ttl_days","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], on the ordinary ","type":"text"},{"code":"tenant <= org","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rule — with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrinkle that ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the second means ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never sweep"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", which is the longest window of all and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is handled by [","type":"text"},{"code":"dcr_ttl_strictness","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", therefore never validated against the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"baseline and never clamped: * [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::default_locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. A language is a presentation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preference; there is no sense in which Italian is stricter than French. *","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::external_client_allowed_resources","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. Each names per-tenant resources — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant’s MCP servers, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" tenant’s callback hosts — and there is no sense in which one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such list is stricter than another. A subset rule would force an organization to enumerate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every tenant’s resource servers in its own baseline before any tenant could name one. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"model’s rule is “a tenant may only be more restrictive”, which binds every field that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"has","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a restrictiveness; a field that has none cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both groups and is checked on the resolved policy rather than on either input: see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"validate_dcr_policy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"OidcPolicy"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"AxiamSDK","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/encode(to:)":{"title":"encode(to:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/encode(to:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"encode","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7EncoderP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/encode(to:)","role":"symbol"}}}